content.thinking:
D5a red as predicted. Now refine the axis selection: velocity-dominant axis. And the reposition must match the axis:

```js
    // One bounce per pass, on the velocity-dominant axis, then push the ball
    // out of the brick it hit so no overlap remains (no sticking).
    const b = hitBricks[0];
    if (Math.abs(ball.vx) > Math.abs(ball.vy)) {
      // Side hit: flip the horizontal axis, keep the vertical one.
      ball.vx = -ball.vx;
      if (ball.vx > 0) ball.x = b.x - ball.r;            // bounced off the left face
      else ball.x = b.x + b.w + ball.r;                  // bounced off the right face
    } else {
      // Top/bottom hit: flip the vertical axis.
      ball.vy = -ball.vy;
      if (ball.vy > 0) ball.y = b.y + b.h + ball.r;      // bounced off the bottom face
      else ball.y = b.y - ball.r;                        // bounced off the top face
    }
```

Wait — careful with the side-hit reposition signs. Ball moving right (vx>0) hits the LEFT face → after flip vx < 0 (moving left) → push the ball LEFT of the brick: ball.x = b.x - r. Ball moving left (vx<0) hits the RIGHT face → flip vx > 0 → push RIGHT: ball.x = b.x + b.w + r. ✓.

For the vertical: ball moving up (vy<0) hits the BOTTOM face → flip vy > 0 (down) → push BELOW: ball.y = b.y + b.h + r ✓. Ball moving down (vy>0) hits the TOP face → flip vy < 0 → push ABOVE: ball.y = b.y - r ✓.

D5a check: vx=300, vy=-100 → |vx| > |vy| → side → vx = -300; ball.x = 244 - 7 = 237. End ball position was (246, 56.33) → pushed to x=237 → ball [230,244] → touches → collides: 244 > 244 false → ✓. vy stays -100 ✓.

D1 check: vx=0, vy=-300 → |vy| > |vx| → vertical → vy = +300, ball.y = 68+7 = 75 ✓.

D3 check: vx=0 → vertical → vy=+300, ball.y=75 ✓.

D2 check: vx=0 → vertical → vy=+710, ball.y = 68+7 = 75 ✓.

Existing wall test: ball (2,200) vx=-300 vy=0: no bricks → hitBricks empty ✓.

Edge: |vx| == |vy| → goes to the vertical branch (tie-break to vertical) — D5b will fix that. For now, D5b is not added yet.

Apply.

